question:
What error is caught by this try-catch?
```javascript
try {
  setTimeout(() => {
    throw new Error('async error');
  }, 0);
} catch (e) {
  console.log('caught:', e.message);
}
```

How can you handle async errors from setTimeout?
```javascript
try {
  const result = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('async error')), 0);
  });
} catch (e) {
  console.log('caught:', e.message);
}
```

What does this error handler do?
```javascript
process.on('uncaughtException', (err) => {
  console.log('caught:', err.message);
});
throw new Error('fatal error');
console.log('after throw');
```

A stream encounters an error. What happens if 'error' is not handled?
```javascript
const readable = fs.createReadStream('missing.txt');
readable.on('data', (chunk) => {
  console.log(chunk);
});
// no error handler
```

How should you handle errors in Express middleware?
```javascript
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(req.body);
  next();
});
```

What is the correct pattern for an Express error handler?
```javascript
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(500).json({error: err.message});
});
```

When a Promise is rejected without a handler, what event is emitted?
```javascript
Promise.reject(new Error('unhandled'));
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  console.log('caught:', reason.message);
});
```

What does error.code tell you in an fs error?
```javascript
fs.readFile('file.txt', (err, data) => {
  if (err && err.code === 'ENOENT') {
    console.log('file not found');
  }
});
```

How do you ensure cleanup after an error?
```javascript
const db = await connectDB();
try {
  const result = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users');
} catch (e) {
  console.error(e);
} finally {
  await db.close();
}
```

What happens if an error handler itself throws an error?
```javascript
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  throw new Error('handler error');
});
```
